From b41eb412555e9cb9f4f6969ae72441171ce0486d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 06:04:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Map browser sorting, filters, downloads, and map
 editing

MapDB 2.0 map gallery backend features from the "New Map Database & Browser"
project:

- Count downloads. `CncMap.download_count` (all time) plus per-day
  `CncMapDownloadStat` rows, incremented with F() expressions so concurrent
  downloads are all counted. No downloader data is stored.
- `GET /maps/<id>/download/` (optionally `?version=N`) for the new UI and
  client integration. The MapDB 1.0 route `/<game>/<sha1>.zip` now counts
  downloads too, and returns 404 for banned maps.
- `/maps/search/` sorting: `popular`, `trending` (downloads within
  MAP_TRENDING_WINDOW_DAYS, default 7), `newest` (new default), `updated`
  (newest file version), plus name/size fields. Fixes a 500 when ordering by
  the old `cnc_map_file__*` fields, which don't exist on CncMap.
- `/maps/search/` filters: `author`, `cnc_user_id`, `category_slug`,
  `min/max_width`, `min/max_height` (newest file version), and
  `created_after/before`.
- `PATCH /maps/<id>/` works now (it raised NotImplementedError). Authors can
  edit name, description, categories, published and incomplete_upload; staff
  can also curate with `is_reviewed`. Staff edits of other users' maps are
  recorded in moderated_by / moderator_notes.
- `manage.py purge_temporary_maps --days N [--dry-run]` removes old,
  unused, anonymous lobby uploads and their files. Keeps banned maps and
  maps that other maps credit as their parent.
- Docs in docs/map_browser.md.
